#!/bin/bash
#
# Prints the setup steps that can't be automated.
set -euo pipefail

cat <<'EOF'

A few things need to be finished by hand:

  * kanata: in System Settings > Privacy & Security, add BOTH `kanata` and
    `kanata-tray` to BOTH Input Monitoring AND Accessibility (all four
    toggles). The LaunchAgent and its sudoers rule are already installed, and
    KeepAlive retries every 20s, so kanata starts on its own once all four
    toggles are granted.

  * iTerm2: Settings > Keys > Key Bindings > Presets > Import, pick
    {{ .chezmoi.workingTree }}/imports/iterm/keybindings.itermkeymap, then
    Settings > Profiles > Other Actions > Import JSON Profiles, pick
    {{ .chezmoi.workingTree }}/imports/iterm/profiles.json, then restart iTerm2.

  * Raycast: Settings > Advanced > Import Settings, pick
    {{ .chezmoi.workingTree }}/imports/raycast.rayconfig.

  * Restart your terminal to pick up the new shell
    configuration.

EOF
